* Sanity check, same as sim/closed-loop-psrr-pex: if .op strayed into the
* wrong equilibrium, fb here will read far from 2.52724e+00. ngspice has no
* ".meas op" analysis type; "print" is this tree's standard way to pull a DC
* operating-point value out of a .control block, parsed by run_pvt_sweep.sh
* from this exact "v(node) = value" line shape.
print v(fb)
print v(sns1)
print v(sns2)
print v(vref)
ac dec 30 1 1e9
* zout_db/zout_phase_deg: v(vref) IS Zout(f) in ohms (real+imag), since
* Itest's AC magnitude is exactly 1A -- db(v(vref)) is therefore
* 20*log10(|Zout|/1 ohm), not a rejection ratio.
let zout_db = db(v(vref))
let zout_phase_deg = cph(v(vref))*180/PI
